OL,3,GNEWSARecord heat leaves flower growers
OL,4,Ashort of blooms
OL,5,
OL,6,FBritish flower growers say the hottest
OL,7,Fsummer on record has cost them entire
OL,8,Fcrops, with some unable to bring
OL,9,Fanything to London markets.
OL,11,FGeorge Stevens, a fourth-generation
OL,12,Fgrower at Stevens of Sibsey in
OL,13,FLincolnshire, lost most of his peony
OL,14,Fseason in May when temperatures jumped
OL,15,Ffrom 14C to 30C ((57 to 86F) within
OL,16,Fdays, and has spent the months since
OL,17,Firrigating ground too dry for seed to
OL,18,Fgerminate.
OL,20,F"It's by far the driest year we've ever
OL,21,Fhad," he tells the BBC at Chiswick
OL,22,FFlower Market on Sunday.
OL,23,APub: 06-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
